For picking up objects you've thrown, there's a patch called
pickup_thrown.  If your copy of nethack is compiled with this
patch applied, you can turn on one option in your .nethackrc,
and then any object you've thrown gets automatically picked
up (if autopickup is on).  If you don't want to apply the patch
and compile nethack yourself, you could play on a public
server that has the patch installed, e.g., nethack.alt.org.

I experimented with pickup_thrown, but I've found that on
the whole I like to have autopickup OFF almost all the time,
because otherwise the game constantly burdens me with
junk I don't want.  The autopickup exceptions I'd need to
set up to fix this are pretty much AI Complete, or at least
much more complex than the available syntax would
support.  Just for example, I only want to auto-pick-up
a pick-axe if it's the first one I've seen in the game that's
not known to be cursed.  I only want to automatically pick
up scrolls and potions if I didn't just drop them in the last
ten turns or so.  I only want to pick up gold if I'm not
burdened and either have less than about 500 gold
(counting what's in containers as well as main inventory)
or have encountered an aligned priest who's still alive.
Meh.  It's easier to just pick things up manually when
I want them.  *I* know when I want to pick things up.

But if you don't mind having autopickup turned on,
you might give pickup_thrown a try.  Like I said, if
you don't want to patch and compile yourself, you
can try it out on a public server like NAO.  Just put
OPTIONS=pickup_thrown in your options file and
Bob, as they say, is your uncle.

(The rest is easy: just create multiple .nethackrc files.)


